,["hs","sc"],["at","and five in Clubs. You need only one more. "],["pg",""],["ls","sc"],["hs","ss"],["at","The Spade suit can provide it "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["hc","sak"],["at","because you can use the @SK to drive out the opponents' @SA "],["pg",""],["lc","sak"],["hc","sq"],["at","and promote your @SQ into a winner."],["pg",""],["lc","sq"],["hs","ss"],["hs","ns"],["nt","\nConsidering the Spade suit by itself, "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["ls","ns"],["hc","skq"],["at","you may be tempted to lead toward your @SK and @SQ "],["pg",""],["lc","skq"],["md","0,s9,,sa"],["hc","sa"],["at","in case East has the @SA. By doing that, you might end up with two tricks in the suit. There are a number of reasons why it is not a good idea on this particular deal."],["pg",""],["lc","sa"],["md","0,sa,,s9"],["hs","ss"],["nt","\nFirst, you don't need two tricks from the Spade suit to make your contract, only one. "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["hs","ns"],["at","Second, you need an entry to get to dummy to lead toward "],["pg",""],["ls","ns"],["hs","ss"],["at","your hand. "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["hc","ha"],["at","The only entry is the @HA. "],["pg",""],["lc","ha"],["hs","sd"],["nt","\nIf, after winning the first trick, "],["pg",""],["ls","sd"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pc","dk"],["pg",""],["hs","sh"],["at","you play a Heart "],["pg",""],["ls","sh"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["hc","ha"],["at","to the @HA "],["pg",""],["lc","ha"],["pc","ha"],["pc","h"],["pg",""],["hs","ns"],["at","before leading Spades, you put the contract in jeopardy. "],["pg",""],["ls","ns"],["pc","s"],["pc","s"],["pc","sk"],["hc","sa"],["at","When the opponents win a trick with the @SA, "],["pg",""],["lc","sa"],["pc","sa"],["pg",""],["hs","eh"],["at","they will be able to take their Heart tricks since you no longer have any way to stop them. In the above layout, East can take four Heart tricks "],["pg",""],["ls","eh"],["hc","ha"],["at","once your @HA is gone, thereby defeating the contract. "],["pg",""],["lc","ha"],["up","8"],["md","0,s9,,sa"],["hc","skq"],["nt","\nFinally, one entry to the dummy is not really enough. To get two Spade tricks, you are going to have to lead twice toward your @SK and @SQ "],["pg",""],["lc","skq"],["hc","sa"],["at","if East (assuming he holds the @SA) plays a small card the first time."],["pg",""],["lc","sa"],["hc","sq"],["nt","\nAll things considered, keep it simple by leading the @SQ "],["pg",""],["lc","sq"],["hc","sk"],["at","or @SK to develop the extra trick you need. "],["pg",""],["lc","sk"],["pc","sk"],["pc","s"],["pc","s"],["pc","sa"],["pg",""],["at","From there on it's clear sailing."],["",""]]}}